
{% assign fallback_content = '' %}
{% case article.handle %}
  {% when 'penya-collective-rooted-in-heritage' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Zimbabwean fashion is a study in contrast: refined tailoring set against vibrant patterning, heritage craft framed by a global lens. From Harare ateliers to emerging runways, designers are defining a visual language that is both rooted and future-facing.</p>
      <h3>Craft As Culture</h3>
      <p>Local craftsmanship sits at the heart of the industry. Beading, woven textiles, and hand-finished details are not accents here; they are the foundation. The result is clothing that carries story, skill, and purpose in every seam.</p>
      <h3>Modern Silhouettes, Ancestral Codes</h3>
      <p>Today's designers are blending sharp, architectural silhouettes with motifs that speak to lineage. Tailored coats, sculptural knitwear, and fluid separates are finished with patterns that nod to place, memory, and identity.</p>
      <h3>Radiance Beyond Borders</h3>
      <p>The momentum is growing, powered by a generation that sees no divide between heritage and innovation. The goal is clear: to shine globally while remaining unmistakably African.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'penya-collective-berlin-contemporary-2027' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Berlin Contemporary 2027 marks a new chapter for Penya Collective: a sharper editorial lens, a broader international audience, and a platform that keeps Zimbabwean design at the center of the conversation.</p>
      <p>The collection direction is intentional. Sculptural shapes, tactile fabrics, and a restrained palette allow craft and construction to lead. The result is a presentation that feels modern in Berlin while remaining grounded in the makers, stories, and cultural codes that shaped it.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'ivhu-tribe-partner-spotlight' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Ivhu Tribe brings a distinct point of view to Penya: expressive pattern, grounded storytelling, and silhouettes that feel both easy and deliberate. Each piece carries a sense of identity without losing wearability.</p>
      <p>What makes the label stand out is its balance. The work feels rooted in place, but never nostalgic. It is a contemporary wardrobe shaped by texture, memory, and confidence.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'haus-of-stone-partner-spotlight' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Haus of Stone approaches fashion with clarity and structure. The label's strength is in its confident lines, polished finishing, and a visual language that feels composed rather than overworked.</p>
      <p>Within Penya, that discipline matters. It expands the collective's range with a sharper expression of modern African luxury - refined, intentional, and built to last beyond a single season.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'by-bakari-partner-spotlight' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>By Bakari channels ease, elegance, and individuality into pieces that feel instantly personal. The label understands how to use color, drape, and proportion to create presence without excess.</p>
      <p>That makes the partnership a natural fit for Penya. It is fashion with personality, but also with discipline - garments that feel vibrant, considered, and confident in motion.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'a-tribe-called-zimbabwe-partner-spotlight' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>A Tribe Called Zimbabwe speaks directly to identity. The label draws energy from local culture, music, and memory, then translates that spirit into clothing that feels bold, current, and unmistakably self-defined.</p>
      <p>In the Penya edit, the work lands as both statement and archive: pieces that celebrate origin while remaining fully engaged with the present moment.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'feli-nandi-partner-spotlight' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Feli Nandi's fashion language carries the same magnetism as her wider creative world: confident, expressive, and rich with personality. The pieces are designed to hold attention through detail rather than volume alone.</p>
      <p>That presence gives the collection its edge. It feels celebratory, but also polished - a strong example of how Penya brings cultural voice into a premium wardrobe context.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'panashe-partner-spotlight' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Panashe designs with softness, precision, and a clear sense of silhouette. The label's work is elegant without feeling distant, and thoughtful without becoming overly formal.</p>
      <p>For Penya, that sensibility adds range to the collective. It offers clients pieces that feel elevated and versatile, with a quiet confidence that rewards a closer look.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% when 'how-we-make-it-production-process' %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Penya's production process is shaped by patience and proximity. Materials are selected with care, sampling is iterative, and makers remain close to every decision that affects fit, finish, and longevity.</p>
      <p>That slower process is deliberate. It protects quality, supports responsible production, and allows each garment to carry the integrity of the hands and studios behind it.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% else %}
    {% capture fallback_content %}
      <p>Penya Journal documents the designers, materials, and cultural conversations shaping the collective. This feature is part of that wider story: contemporary African fashion presented with clarity, care, and context.</p>
      <p>For more on the collection, the makers, or how to order, contact Penya client care and the team will guide you directly.</p>
    {% endcapture %}
{% endcase %}

<div class="blog-post-content rte">
  <rte-formatter>
    {% if article.content != blank %}
      {{ article.content }}
    {% elsif fallback_content != blank %}
      {{ fallback_content }}
    {% endif %}
  </rte-formatter>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .blog-post-content {
    max-width: var(--normal-content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.content",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:names.content"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
